# Database Migration Safety Rules (Conditional)

- Apply `eng-databases` before editing schemas or migrations.
- Preserve production data: never drop columns/tables or rewrite historical migrations without explicit human approval and verified backup/rollback scripts.
- Wrap schema migrations in explicit transactions where supported, add indexes cleanly, and verify foreign key / uniqueness constraints with isolated tests.
- Keep live DB connection strings out of source and factory memory; document variable names only in `.env.example`.
